{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry and no Integrator feedback yet, so this is a baseline built from the contract rather than from evidence. The 25 mm tape is covered by five 12 mm sensors spaced 12 mm apart (x = -0.024 to +0.024), so at least two sensors always see the line edge while the tape stays within about 25 mm of centre. The sensors sit 0.04 m ahead of the axle, far enough that the steering signal leads the wheels and gives the controller time to react at the base speeds needed to finish in 3 s. Wheel track 0.12 m and wheel radius 0.03 m give a moderate turn authority without excessive yaw inertia. Mass 0.6 kg keeps acceleration high for the 1.5 m/s average speed target. Body width 0.12 m sets the off-track limit at 0.06 m (the floor), which is the most generous limit available at this body size. I expect the baseline to complete the development tracks with a small RMS error if the Integrator's controller can use a symmetric five-sensor signal. I have not yet tested whether a wider or narrower sensor span, or a different forward offset, helps on the sharper bends. Those are the first things to test once evidence arrives.",
  "intent": "Baseline symmetric platform: five 12 mm sensors across x = ±0.024 m with 12 mm pitch, placed 0.04 m ahead of the axle, on a 0.12 m track with 0.03 m wheels, 0.6 kg mass and 0.12 m body width. Kept deliberately simple so the Integrator has a clean reference to tune against. Expect completion on the oval and s-bend tracks; the slalom may show higher RMS error and more line-loss events. Considering next (not committed): a narrower sensor span (±0.012 m) to reduce noise sensitivity, and a forward offset of 0.06 m to increase steering lead if oscillation shows up.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "feedback_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "noise_robustness"]
  },
  "learning": "Baseline with no race evidence yet. The first race will show whether five 12 mm sensors at 12 mm pitch resolve the line edge well enough for the Integrator's controller, and whether the 0.04 m forward offset gives enough steering lead. Revise sensor span and forward offset based on rms_error, max_error and steering_oscillation from the race."
}
